{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedAddable","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedAddable","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedShapeRun","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedTableau"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_append_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_append_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L404-L412","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_append_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_append_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L397-L402","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCellSteps_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCellSteps_nil","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L384-L389","doc":"**The count shape, from the empty shape** — the form the bridge will use, with the starting\nshape gone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_addCellSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_addCellSteps","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L377-L382","doc":"The built shape has exactly the rows that were used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCellSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCellSteps","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L362-L375","doc":"**Row `i` of the built shape counts the steps that landed in row `i`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_of_getD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_of_getD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L356-L360","doc":"A nonzero entry is in range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L347-L349","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L341-L345","doc":"**The insertion-built case, closed.** Both of brick 18's hypotheses now come from brick 20's\nmachinery rather than from brick 19's iff — an independent route to the same conclusion, which is\nwhat makes the two shape-level pictures agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_rowIndices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_rowIndices","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L329-L339","doc":"**A whole insertion run is an addable sequence, and it builds the shape.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isAddable_newRowIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isAddable_newRowIndex","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L308-L327","doc":"**Insertion adds an addable cell.**\n\nNot proved from the bumping-column argument directly — it is read off the fact that `insert`\npreserves `ColStrict` (`insert_colStrict`, already in the corpus), whose shape is therefore weakly\ndecreasing. Spelling that out at the added index *is* addability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.newRowIndex_le","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L295-L306","doc":"The row insertion appends to is within the shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_insert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_insert","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L280-L293","doc":"**Insertion acts on shapes as `addCell`** — the mirror of brick 17's `tableauShape_uninsert`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_cons_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell_cons_succ","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L271-L278","doc":"Adding below the top row leaves the top row alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_and_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_and_empty","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L258-L263","doc":"**Both of brick 18's hypotheses, from an addable sequence out of the empty shape.** This is the\nform the recording tableau will supply: a standard `Q` is an addable sequence, and the shape it\nbuilds is the shape of `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.youngShape_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.youngShape_nil","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L255-L256","doc":"**The empty shape is a Young shape** — the starting point for a whole run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_of_addable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_of_addable","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L249-L253","doc":"The corner condition, on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_addCellSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shapeCornersAlong_addCellSteps","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L229-L247","doc":"**An addable sequence peels back as corners, exactly onto where it started.**\n\nBoth halves come out of one induction: the corner at step `i` is `isCorner_addCell` applied at the\nshape the *later* steps peel back to, which is what the inductive hypothesis's second half supplies.\nWithout that half the corner check would have nothing to stand on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_cons","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L226-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_nil","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L224-L224","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.AddableAlong","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.AddableAlong","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L219-L222","doc":"**Every step of `is` adds an addable cell** to the shape as it stands at that step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_cons","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L216-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps_nil","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCellSteps","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L209-L212","doc":"Build a shape by adding the cells named by `is`, in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCorner_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.removeCorner_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L187-L207","doc":"**Peeling the added cell returns the shape you started from.** This is what makes the run-level\nstatement an exact inverse rather than merely a corner condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L175-L185","doc":"**The added cell is a corner of the result.**\n\nThe shape-level mirror of brick 15's `insert_isCorner`, with the same one-line reason: the row below\nwas already bounded by the row's *old* length, so after the increment it is strictly shorter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.youngShape_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.youngShape_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L139-L173","doc":"Adding an addable cell keeps the shape a Young shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_of_getD_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_of_getD_step","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L120-L137","doc":"A shape is weakly decreasing as soon as each adjacent step is. The positional form is what the\n`addCell` case analysis produces, so this is the bridge back to `List.Sorted`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCell_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCell_ne","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L107-L118","doc":"Every other position is untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCell_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_addCell_self","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L97-L105","doc":"The entry at the added position goes up by one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_length_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L88-L95","doc":"The added position is in range afterwards. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.IsAddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.IsAddable","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L83-L86","doc":"Row `i` is **addable**: in range or exactly one past the end, and strictly shorter than the row\nabove it (vacuous at the top row). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addCell","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L78-L81","doc":"**Add a cell to row `i`.** In range this lengthens row `i`; one past the end it starts a new row\nof length one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_succ_le_of_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_succ_le_of_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L61-L76","doc":"Row lengths do not increase, read with `getD` so out-of-range indices behave (both sides `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.YoungShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.YoungShape","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L58-L59","doc":"A **Young shape**: row lengths weakly decreasing and all positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_past","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_past","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedAddable.lean#L54-L56","doc":"Reading past the end of a shape gives `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}